  "historical_output_text": " The detail can include sensory details or something as mundane as signage.\n\nI always took this park, a stone’s-\tthrow distance from downtown Manhattan in Soho and a ten-block trek on city roads, in stride without really seeing what I saw every morning or what I was about as well.\n\nOn any morning I passed along these paths I had walked since the first snow melted last February and into springtime and then summer again. There are times I pass in solitude. There was one time when there might as just be two or a couple others and I had the feeling of the morning all to mine and it seemed a gift to know no-one was about me in my morning reveres, no matter that they might as likely have known no me. And yet on other times my presence seemed to count as little, as the park’s. On other walks there",
